  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "annot-zoho-sign-2b-s4-20260724",
   "x": 70,
   "y": 2180,
   "width": 880,
   "height": 205,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (Provider swap Adobe->Zoho, 2B-S4): the credential-free signature FACADE\nin adobe-sign.ts now branches on provider - getSignatureProvider('zoho-sign') -> makeZohoSignatureProvider\nover the live ZohoSignBackend, 'cmd' -> the inactive Autenticacao.Gov seam, default/'adobe' -> the Adobe\nfacade (notConnectedBackend). The pluggable POST /api/signature/send route is injected BOTH backends from\nserver.ts (zohoBackend built before the adobe router mount); the ERP itself signs via /api/zoho-sign/*\ndirectly. shared/served-app.ts signatureSend gains REAL zod schemas (SignatureSendRequest/Response,\nshrink-only passthrough) replacing z.unknown(). Zoho is the sole live e-sign provider; Adobe stays\nfacade-only, proven by salomao-erp-zoho-swap.e2e.mjs (/api/zoho-sign present + used, /api/adobe-sign facade).",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (Provider swap Adobe->Zoho, 2B-S4): the credential-free signature FACADE\nin adobe-sign.ts now branches on provider - getSignatureProvider('zoho-sign') -> makeZohoSignatureProvider\nover the live ZohoSignBackend, 'cmd' -> the inactive Autenticacao.Gov seam, default/'adobe' -> the Adobe\nfacade (notConnectedBackend). The pluggable POST /api/signature/send route is injected BOTH backends from\nserver.ts (zohoBackend built before the adobe router mount); the ERP itself signs via /api/zoho-sign/*\ndirectly. shared/served-app.ts signatureSend gains REAL zod schemas (SignatureSendRequest/Response,\nshrink-only passthrough) replacing z.unknown(). Zoho is the sole live e-sign provider; Adobe stays\nfacade-only, proven by salomao-erp-zoho-swap.e2e.mjs (/api/zoho-sign present + used, /api/adobe-sign facade).",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-24 (Provider swap Adobe->Zoho, 2B-S4): the credential-free signature FACADE\nin adobe-sign.ts now branches on provider - getSignatureProvider('zoho-sign') -> makeZohoSignatureProvider\nover the live ZohoSignBackend, 'cmd' -> the inactive Autenticacao.Gov seam, default/'adobe' -> the Adobe\nfacade (notConnectedBackend). The pluggable POST /api/signature/send route is injected BOTH backends from\nserver.ts (zohoBackend built before the adobe router mount); the ERP itself signs via /api/zoho-sign/*\ndirectly. shared/served-app.ts signatureSend gains REAL zod schemas (SignatureSendRequest/Response,\nshrink-only passthrough) replacing z.unknown(). Zoho is the sole live e-sign provider; Adobe stays\nfacade-only, proven by salomao-erp-zoho-swap.e2e.mjs (/api/zoho-sign present + used, /api/adobe-sign facade).",
