  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "annot-security-cofre-phase0-20260727",
   "x": 70,
   "y": 3784.5,
   "width": 980,
   "height": 600,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-27 (NEW MODULE api/src/security/ - Cofre discovery-gate Phase 0 remediation).\nA new top-level tier-neutral module, registered in the .eslintrc.cjs module-direction zone array\nalongside data/auth/llm/... (so nothing in it may import routes/ or server.ts). It holds the two\ncontrols that were previously either duplicated or absent, and it imports only services/ and node:\nbuiltins - no domain module depends on it in the other direction.\n\nredaction.ts - THE value-keyed masker. Collapses two divergent private copies:\nintegrations/http-template.ts (which emitted ***...1234, a persisted plaintext SUFFIX of every\ncredential) and automation/executors/api-call.ts (raw-literal match only, so URL-encoded/base64/\nJSON-escaped occurrences reached the persisted step record). Run-scoped SecretRegistry ->\n[REDACTED:<handle>], no fragment and no length hint; both former copies are now thin callers.\nautomation/run-events.ts takes an OPTIONAL registry - its header claimed payloads were 'already\nredacted at the executor', true only of api_call, so every other step type reached SSE unfiltered.\n\npath-containment.ts - copy-with-review of ekoa-bridge/src/containment/resolver.ts (ADR-001), which\nthe DAEMON has had since 2026-07-10 while the CORTEX side had nothing: automation/\nplatform-primitives.ts resolveUserPath was 'if (isAbsolute(path)) return path;', giving a\nMODEL-authored ekoa_action recipe unrestricted file.read/file.write on the API host with the bytes\nlanding in persisted capturedValues and the calling agent's tool result. Now rooted per owner at\n<dataDir>/action-workspace/<orgId>/<userId>, real-path checked, symlink-escape proof, write-safe\nfor not-yet-created leaves, plus a credential-bearing denylist applied to the REAL path.\n\norigin-binding.ts - credential-to-origin binding (I6). An SSRF guard answers 'is this host\ninfrastructure I must not touch'; it CANNOT answer 'may this host see THIS credential'. api_call\ninterpolated a decrypted credential into a MODEL-authored URL behind only guardedFetch, which\npermits every public host by design. credentialedFetch/assertOriginAllowed make allowedOrigins a\nREQUIRED option that refuses when empty. NEW SEAM automation/seams.ts setIntegrationOriginResolver,\nbound in server.ts from the integration's own declared base URLs, DEFAULT REFUSE - Cofre per-item\nboundOrigins replaces the derivation in WS-C without moving the enforcement point.\nintegrations/action-executor.ts also moves off bare globalThis.fetch onto guardedFetch.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-27 (NEW MODULE api/src/security/ - Cofre discovery-gate Phase 0 remediation).\nA new top-level tier-neutral module, registered in the .eslintrc.cjs module-direction zone array\nalongside data/auth/llm/... (so nothing in it may import routes/ or server.ts). It holds the two\ncontrols that were previously either duplicated or absent, and it imports only services/ and node:\nbuiltins - no domain module depends on it in the other direction.\n\nredaction.ts - THE value-keyed masker. Collapses two divergent private copies:\nintegrations/http-template.ts (which emitted ***...1234, a persisted plaintext SUFFIX of every\ncredential) and automation/executors/api-call.ts (raw-literal match only, so URL-encoded/base64/\nJSON-escaped occurrences reached the persisted step record). Run-scoped SecretRegistry ->\n[REDACTED:<handle>], no fragment and no length hint; both former copies are now thin callers.\nautomation/run-events.ts takes an OPTIONAL registry - its header claimed payloads were 'already\nredacted at the executor', true only of api_call, so every other step type reached SSE unfiltered.\n\npath-containment.ts - copy-with-review of ekoa-bridge/src/containment/resolver.ts (ADR-001), which\nthe DAEMON has had since 2026-07-10 while the CORTEX side had nothing: automation/\nplatform-primitives.ts resolveUserPath was 'if (isAbsolute(path)) return path;', giving a\nMODEL-authored ekoa_action recipe unrestricted file.read/file.write on the API host with the bytes\nlanding in persisted capturedValues and the calling agent's tool result. Now rooted per owner at\n<dataDir>/action-workspace/<orgId>/<userId>, real-path checked, symlink-escape proof, write-safe\nfor not-yet-created leaves, plus a credential-bearing denylist applied to the REAL path.\n\norigin-binding.ts - credential-to-origin binding (I6). An SSRF guard answers 'is this host\ninfrastructure I must not touch'; it CANNOT answer 'may this host see THIS credential'. api_call\ninterpolated a decrypted credential into a MODEL-authored URL behind only guardedFetch, which\npermits every public host by design. credentialedFetch/assertOriginAllowed make allowedOrigins a\nREQUIRED option that refuses when empty. NEW SEAM automation/seams.ts setIntegrationOriginResolver,\nbound in server.ts from the integration's own declared base URLs, DEFAULT REFUSE - Cofre per-item\nboundOrigins replaces the derivation in WS-C without moving the enforcement point.\nintegrations/action-executor.ts also moves off bare globalThis.fetch onto guardedFetch.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-27 (NEW MODULE api/src/security/ - Cofre discovery-gate Phase 0 remediation).\nA new top-level tier-neutral module, registered in the .eslintrc.cjs module-direction zone array\nalongside data/auth/llm/... (so nothing in it may import routes/ or server.ts). It holds the two\ncontrols that were previously either duplicated or absent, and it imports only services/ and node:\nbuiltins - no domain module depends on it in the other direction.\n\nredaction.ts - THE value-keyed masker. Collapses two divergent private copies:\nintegrations/http-template.ts (which emitted ***...1234, a persisted plaintext SUFFIX of every\ncredential) and automation/executors/api-call.ts (raw-literal match only, so URL-encoded/base64/\nJSON-escaped occurrences reached the persisted step record). Run-scoped SecretRegistry ->\n[REDACTED:<handle>], no fragment and no length hint; both former copies are now thin callers.\nautomation/run-events.ts takes an OPTIONAL registry - its header claimed payloads were 'already\nredacted at the executor', true only of api_call, so every other step type reached SSE unfiltered.\n\npath-containment.ts - copy-with-review of ekoa-bridge/src/containment/resolver.ts (ADR-001), which\nthe DAEMON has had since 2026-07-10 while the CORTEX side had nothing: automation/\nplatform-primitives.ts resolveUserPath was 'if (isAbsolute(path)) return path;', giving a\nMODEL-authored ekoa_action recipe unrestricted file.read/file.write on the API host with the bytes\nlanding in persisted capturedValues and the calling agent's tool result. Now rooted per owner at\n<dataDir>/action-workspace/<orgId>/<userId>, real-path checked, symlink-escape proof, write-safe\nfor not-yet-created leaves, plus a credential-bearing denylist applied to the REAL path.\n\norigin-binding.ts - credential-to-origin binding (I6). An SSRF guard answers 'is this host\ninfrastructure I must not touch'; it CANNOT answer 'may this host see THIS credential'. api_call\ninterpolated a decrypted credential into a MODEL-authored URL behind only guardedFetch, which\npermits every public host by design. credentialedFetch/assertOriginAllowed make allowedOrigins a\nREQUIRED option that refuses when empty. NEW SEAM automation/seams.ts setIntegrationOriginResolver,\nbound in server.ts from the integration's own declared base URLs, DEFAULT REFUSE - Cofre per-item\nboundOrigins replaces the derivation in WS-C without moving the enforcement point.\nintegrations/action-executor.ts also moves off bare globalThis.fetch onto guardedFetch.",
