  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "annot-cortex-cli-e7-4b21c8de",
   "x": 70,
   "y": 7450,
   "width": 916,
   "height": 332.5,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (cortex CLI + generated typed client, slice E7): the repository grows a FOURTH\ntop-level zone - clients/ (npm workspace glob \"clients/*\"), holding clients/cortex-cli. It is a CONSUMER,\nnot a module: nothing in api/, web/ or shared/ may import it, and it may import shared/ (the contract)\nplus its own generated client ONLY. New eslint import/no-restricted-paths zones enforce both directions\n(clients/*/src|bin -> api|web forbidden; api|web|shared -> clients forbidden). The one carve-out is\nclients/*/tests, a dev-only harness that boots the api routers in-process to drive the built binary -\nthe same shape that lets api/tests import server.ts under the module-direction zone.\nTHE CLIENT IS GENERATED, NEVER HAND-WRITTEN: scripts/generate-client.mjs reads docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json\nand emits src/generated/cortex-v1.d.ts (openapi-typescript, OpenAPI 3.1) plus src/generated/operations.ts -\nthe runtime table a .d.ts cannot carry: method, path template, x-ekoa-success-statuses IN ORDER, kind +\nmedia type, timeout. Both are committed and diffed by scripts/check-client-drift.mjs (root gate:client-drift,\nin ci:lane), closing the chain shared/ descriptors -> OpenAPI spec -> generated client with no quiet link.\nONE WRAPPER: src/client.ts is the only file in the package that speaks HTTP - URL assembly, the bearer key,\nthe trace-only X-Client header, the per-operation timeout, the shared ErrorEnvelope and the binary\napplication/x-tar path live there once. Commands (src/commands/{memory,knowledge,automations}.ts) name an\noperationId and hand over typed slots; a hand-written per-capability HTTP call is a review failure.\nCONTRACT SEMANTICS THE CLIENT PRESERVES: automations.createRun answers 202 fresh / 200 idempotent replay,\nsurfaced as created/replayed; automations.create is 201; memvault.exportVault is bytes, never JSON; and the\nrun SSE stream is session-only, so watch polls. Nothing about the provider moved for this slice.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (cortex CLI + generated typed client, slice E7): the repository grows a FOURTH\ntop-level zone - clients/ (npm workspace glob \"clients/*\"), holding clients/cortex-cli. It is a CONSUMER,\nnot a module: nothing in api/, web/ or shared/ may import it, and it may import shared/ (the contract)\nplus its own generated client ONLY. New eslint import/no-restricted-paths zones enforce both directions\n(clients/*/src|bin -> api|web forbidden; api|web|shared -> clients forbidden). The one carve-out is\nclients/*/tests, a dev-only harness that boots the api routers in-process to drive the built binary -\nthe same shape that lets api/tests import server.ts under the module-direction zone.\nTHE CLIENT IS GENERATED, NEVER HAND-WRITTEN: scripts/generate-client.mjs reads docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json\nand emits src/generated/cortex-v1.d.ts (openapi-typescript, OpenAPI 3.1) plus src/generated/operations.ts -\nthe runtime table a .d.ts cannot carry: method, path template, x-ekoa-success-statuses IN ORDER, kind +\nmedia type, timeout. Both are committed and diffed by scripts/check-client-drift.mjs (root gate:client-drift,\nin ci:lane), closing the chain shared/ descriptors -> OpenAPI spec -> generated client with no quiet link.\nONE WRAPPER: src/client.ts is the only file in the package that speaks HTTP - URL assembly, the bearer key,\nthe trace-only X-Client header, the per-operation timeout, the shared ErrorEnvelope and the binary\napplication/x-tar path live there once. Commands (src/commands/{memory,knowledge,automations}.ts) name an\noperationId and hand over typed slots; a hand-written per-capability HTTP call is a review failure.\nCONTRACT SEMANTICS THE CLIENT PRESERVES: automations.createRun answers 202 fresh / 200 idempotent replay,\nsurfaced as created/replayed; automations.create is 201; memvault.exportVault is bytes, never JSON; and the\nrun SSE stream is session-only, so watch polls. Nothing about the provider moved for this slice.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-07-31 (cortex CLI + generated typed client, slice E7): the repository grows a FOURTH\ntop-level zone - clients/ (npm workspace glob \"clients/*\"), holding clients/cortex-cli. It is a CONSUMER,\nnot a module: nothing in api/, web/ or shared/ may import it, and it may import shared/ (the contract)\nplus its own generated client ONLY. New eslint import/no-restricted-paths zones enforce both directions\n(clients/*/src|bin -> api|web forbidden; api|web|shared -> clients forbidden). The one carve-out is\nclients/*/tests, a dev-only harness that boots the api routers in-process to drive the built binary -\nthe same shape that lets api/tests import server.ts under the module-direction zone.\nTHE CLIENT IS GENERATED, NEVER HAND-WRITTEN: scripts/generate-client.mjs reads docs/openapi/cortex.v1.json\nand emits src/generated/cortex-v1.d.ts (openapi-typescript, OpenAPI 3.1) plus src/generated/operations.ts -\nthe runtime table a .d.ts cannot carry: method, path template, x-ekoa-success-statuses IN ORDER, kind +\nmedia type, timeout. Both are committed and diffed by scripts/check-client-drift.mjs (root gate:client-drift,\nin ci:lane), closing the chain shared/ descriptors -> OpenAPI spec -> generated client with no quiet link.\nONE WRAPPER: src/client.ts is the only file in the package that speaks HTTP - URL assembly, the bearer key,\nthe trace-only X-Client header, the per-operation timeout, the shared ErrorEnvelope and the binary\napplication/x-tar path live there once. Commands (src/commands/{memory,knowledge,automations}.ts) name an\noperationId and hand over typed slots; a hand-written per-capability HTTP call is a review failure.\nCONTRACT SEMANTICS THE CLIENT PRESERVES: automations.createRun answers 202 fresh / 200 idempotent replay,\nsurfaced as created/replayed; automations.create is 201; memvault.exportVault is bytes, never JSON; and the\nrun SSE stream is session-only, so watch polls. Nothing about the provider moved for this slice.",
