  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "annot-automation-primitives-20260818",
   "x": 60,
   "y": 14914.5,
   "width": 1060,
   "height": 507.5,
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (automation primitives: budgets.ts + origin-posture.ts). TWO NEW tier-5 modules\ninside automation/, both imported by engine.ts, neither adding a module EDGE (origin-posture reads the\nintegrations/ declaration through a STRUCTURAL type - the schedules/supervisor.ts pattern - so\nautomation/ still reaches integrations/ only through seams wired at the composition root).\n\nautomation/budgets.ts - THE knob module. REHEARSAL_BUDGET moved here verbatim from rehearsal.ts\n(re-exported there, so no call site churned; values pinned by tests/automation/budgets.test.ts) and\ngains three siblings. STEP_RETRY_BUDGET: one deterministic re-attempt of the SAME resolved action\nbefore any vision/fixer escalation, and the cache-then-vision re-ground now COUNTED per step INDEX\nthrough a per-run StepRetryLedger threaded into executeStep (it was an invisible catch before, so a\nstep index the fixer kept revisiting bought a fresh model call every visit). NORMAL_RUN_BUDGET: a\nnormal run had NO wall-clock cap at all - 8 min, minus pausedTotalMs so a long human ceremony never\ntrips it, surfacing through the EXISTING runError -> terminal failed path and manufacturing no\nrehearsal summary; each mode now reads its own pause cap. DISCOVERY_BUDGET: declared, NO consumer\n(discovery is P2).\n\nautomation/origin-posture.ts - permissive vs adversarial, DEFAULT ADVERSARIAL/CLOSED, resolved AT USE\nfrom a new additive optional per-action declaration on IntegrationAction (posture?, authProfile?, in\nintegrations/definitions.ts; deliberately NOT in shared/, same reason as backingType). Nothing stores a\nresolved value - the discipline the deleted declaredOrigins field left behind. cloudEgressAllowed is\nclamped in the ONE constructor and the result frozen, so adversarial+cloud is unconstructible rather\nthan merely discouraged; and a permissive label cannot follow an action off the origin its httpConfig\nnames. resolveTargetPosture records the precedence decision (plan trap T9): POSTURE WINS over\nresolveStepDeclaration's target:'cloud' default, so a legacy declaration-free automation does not\nsilently earn cloud egress against an adversarial site. NO consumer wired yet - P4 (egress opt-in +\nbridge-only routing) and P3.3 (typist vs attended re-auth) consume it rather than re-deciding.\nSuites: tests/automation/budgets.test.ts + origin-posture.test.ts (incl. a compile-time pin that the\nposture union stays identical on both sides of the tier boundary), and the 'run budgets' block in\ntests/automation/engine.test.ts.",
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (automation primitives: budgets.ts + origin-posture.ts). TWO NEW tier-5 modules\ninside automation/, both imported by engine.ts, neither adding a module EDGE (origin-posture reads the\nintegrations/ declaration through a STRUCTURAL type - the schedules/supervisor.ts pattern - so\nautomation/ still reaches integrations/ only through seams wired at the composition root).\n\nautomation/budgets.ts - THE knob module. REHEARSAL_BUDGET moved here verbatim from rehearsal.ts\n(re-exported there, so no call site churned; values pinned by tests/automation/budgets.test.ts) and\ngains three siblings. STEP_RETRY_BUDGET: one deterministic re-attempt of the SAME resolved action\nbefore any vision/fixer escalation, and the cache-then-vision re-ground now COUNTED per step INDEX\nthrough a per-run StepRetryLedger threaded into executeStep (it was an invisible catch before, so a\nstep index the fixer kept revisiting bought a fresh model call every visit). NORMAL_RUN_BUDGET: a\nnormal run had NO wall-clock cap at all - 8 min, minus pausedTotalMs so a long human ceremony never\ntrips it, surfacing through the EXISTING runError -> terminal failed path and manufacturing no\nrehearsal summary; each mode now reads its own pause cap. DISCOVERY_BUDGET: declared, NO consumer\n(discovery is P2).\n\nautomation/origin-posture.ts - permissive vs adversarial, DEFAULT ADVERSARIAL/CLOSED, resolved AT USE\nfrom a new additive optional per-action declaration on IntegrationAction (posture?, authProfile?, in\nintegrations/definitions.ts; deliberately NOT in shared/, same reason as backingType). Nothing stores a\nresolved value - the discipline the deleted declaredOrigins field left behind. cloudEgressAllowed is\nclamped in the ONE constructor and the result frozen, so adversarial+cloud is unconstructible rather\nthan merely discouraged; and a permissive label cannot follow an action off the origin its httpConfig\nnames. resolveTargetPosture records the precedence decision (plan trap T9): POSTURE WINS over\nresolveStepDeclaration's target:'cloud' default, so a legacy declaration-free automation does not\nsilently earn cloud egress against an adversarial site. NO consumer wired yet - P4 (egress opt-in +\nbridge-only routing) and P3.3 (typist vs attended re-auth) consume it rather than re-deciding.\nSuites: tests/automation/budgets.test.ts + origin-posture.test.ts (incl. a compile-time pin that the\nposture union stays identical on both sides of the tier boundary), and the 'run budgets' block in\ntests/automation/engine.test.ts.",
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (automation primitives: budgets.ts + origin-posture.ts). TWO NEW tier-5 modules\ninside automation/, both imported by engine.ts, neither adding a module EDGE (origin-posture reads the\nintegrations/ declaration through a STRUCTURAL type - the schedules/supervisor.ts pattern - so\nautomation/ still reaches integrations/ only through seams wired at the composition root).\n\nautomation/budgets.ts - THE knob module. REHEARSAL_BUDGET moved here verbatim from rehearsal.ts\n(re-exported there, so no call site churned; values pinned by tests/automation/budgets.test.ts) and\ngains three siblings. STEP_RETRY_BUDGET: one deterministic re-attempt of the SAME resolved action\nbefore any vision/fixer escalation, and the cache-then-vision re-ground now COUNTED per step INDEX\nthrough a per-run StepRetryLedger threaded into executeStep (it was an invisible catch before, so a\nstep index the fixer kept revisiting bought a fresh model call every visit). NORMAL_RUN_BUDGET: a\nnormal run had NO wall-clock cap at all - 8 min, minus pausedTotalMs so a long human ceremony never\ntrips it, surfacing through the EXISTING runError -> terminal failed path and manufacturing no\nrehearsal summary; each mode now reads its own pause cap. DISCOVERY_BUDGET: declared, NO consumer\n(discovery is P2).\n\nautomation/origin-posture.ts - permissive vs adversarial, DEFAULT ADVERSARIAL/CLOSED, resolved AT USE\nfrom a new additive optional per-action declaration on IntegrationAction (posture?, authProfile?, in\nintegrations/definitions.ts; deliberately NOT in shared/, same reason as backingType). Nothing stores a\nresolved value - the discipline the deleted declaredOrigins field left behind. cloudEgressAllowed is\nclamped in the ONE constructor and the result frozen, so adversarial+cloud is unconstructible rather\nthan merely discouraged; and a permissive label cannot follow an action off the origin its httpConfig\nnames. resolveTargetPosture records the precedence decision (plan trap T9): POSTURE WINS over\nresolveStepDeclaration's target:'cloud' default, so a legacy declaration-free automation does not\nsilently earn cloud egress against an adversarial site. NO consumer wired yet - P4 (egress opt-in +\nbridge-only routing) and P3.3 (typist vs attended re-auth) consume it rather than re-deciding.\nSuites: tests/automation/budgets.test.ts + origin-posture.test.ts (incl. a compile-time pin that the\nposture union stays identical on both sides of the tier boundary), and the 'run budgets' block in\ntests/automation/engine.test.ts.",
