   "locked": false,
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (clients/bridge): the ekoa-bridge daemon moves in as a THIRD workspace package\nbeside clients/cortex-cli - a content copy, never a history import, so its own CLAUDE.md and .claude/\nskills stayed behind. It is a SEPARATE PROCESS, not a module: nothing in api/ imports it, it is absent\nfrom the root build (shared+api+web), and the clients/* import-boundary zone forbids it reaching api/\nor web/ - so Playwright can never bundle into the api server. It reaches Cortex the way any machine\ndoes, over the WS bridge (api/src/bridge/), and its only in-repo dependency is @ekoa/shared.\nThe vendored wire copy is GONE: clients/bridge/src/wire/index.ts re-exports BridgeFrame/DelegatedTask/\nDelegationResult/EgressLedgerRow/BridgeCapability/canonicalTaskBinding straight from @ekoa/shared, so\ndaemon and Cortex parse the same objects and sign the same bytes by construction. The drift test that\npoliced the copy was deleted rather than ported - drift is now impossible, not merely detected. Only\nwire/signing.ts stays local (the HMAC wrappers shared does not carry).\nToolchain: DOWNGRADED to the monorepo's (root ESLint 8 .eslintrc.cjs, TS 5.x, @types/node 20, inherited\nvitest), per the cortex-cli precedent - no own eslint/ts/vitest devDeps. The daemon's custom\nfs-containment lint rules came WITH it as Rule 4 of .eslintrc.cjs (single-resolver invariant), proven\nby clients/bridge/test/lint/containment-rule.test.ts against the ROOT config.\nCI: the daemon's cross-repo workflow folds into ci.yml. Its unit lane rides the workspace test fan-out;\nits heavy canary (mongodb-memory-server + api/dist + the real WS server) is an explicit step after\n`npm run build`, behind a guard asserting the harness entrypoints exist - without it a missing api/dist\nturns the suite into describe.skip and the step passes having tested nothing.\nPackaging: the shipped .tgz cannot resolve the `*` workspace dep and needs shared's RUNTIME (zod values,\nnot just types), so `npm run pack:dist` esbuild-bundles @ekoa/shared into dist/cli/index.js from a\nstaging tree; tsc -b stays what CI typechecks. Everything else stays external and installs on the laptop.",
   "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (clients/bridge): the ekoa-bridge daemon moves in as a THIRD workspace package\nbeside clients/cortex-cli - a content copy, never a history import, so its own CLAUDE.md and .claude/\nskills stayed behind. It is a SEPARATE PROCESS, not a module: nothing in api/ imports it, it is absent\nfrom the root build (shared+api+web), and the clients/* import-boundary zone forbids it reaching api/\nor web/ - so Playwright can never bundle into the api server. It reaches Cortex the way any machine\ndoes, over the WS bridge (api/src/bridge/), and its only in-repo dependency is @ekoa/shared.\nThe vendored wire copy is GONE: clients/bridge/src/wire/index.ts re-exports BridgeFrame/DelegatedTask/\nDelegationResult/EgressLedgerRow/BridgeCapability/canonicalTaskBinding straight from @ekoa/shared, so\ndaemon and Cortex parse the same objects and sign the same bytes by construction. The drift test that\npoliced the copy was deleted rather than ported - drift is now impossible, not merely detected. Only\nwire/signing.ts stays local (the HMAC wrappers shared does not carry).\nToolchain: DOWNGRADED to the monorepo's (root ESLint 8 .eslintrc.cjs, TS 5.x, @types/node 20, inherited\nvitest), per the cortex-cli precedent - no own eslint/ts/vitest devDeps. The daemon's custom\nfs-containment lint rules came WITH it as Rule 4 of .eslintrc.cjs (single-resolver invariant), proven\nby clients/bridge/test/lint/containment-rule.test.ts against the ROOT config.\nCI: the daemon's cross-repo workflow folds into ci.yml. Its unit lane rides the workspace test fan-out;\nits heavy canary (mongodb-memory-server + api/dist + the real WS server) is an explicit step after\n`npm run build`, behind a guard asserting the harness entrypoints exist - without it a missing api/dist\nturns the suite into describe.skip and the step passes having tested nothing.\nPackaging: the shipped .tgz cannot resolve the `*` workspace dep and needs shared's RUNTIME (zod values,\nnot just types), so `npm run pack:dist` esbuild-bundles @ekoa/shared into dist/cli/index.js from a\nstaging tree; tsc -b stays what CI typechecks. Everything else stays external and installs on the laptop.",
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (clients/bridge): the ekoa-bridge daemon moves in as a THIRD workspace package\nbeside clients/cortex-cli - a content copy, never a history import, so its own CLAUDE.md and .claude/\nskills stayed behind. It is a SEPARATE PROCESS, not a module: nothing in api/ imports it, it is absent\nfrom the root build (shared+api+web), and the clients/* import-boundary zone forbids it reaching api/\nor web/ - so Playwright can never bundle into the api server. It reaches Cortex the way any machine\ndoes, over the WS bridge (api/src/bridge/), and its only in-repo dependency is @ekoa/shared.\nThe vendored wire copy is GONE: clients/bridge/src/wire/index.ts re-exports BridgeFrame/DelegatedTask/\nDelegationResult/EgressLedgerRow/BridgeCapability/canonicalTaskBinding straight from @ekoa/shared, so\ndaemon and Cortex parse the same objects and sign the same bytes by construction. The drift test that\npoliced the copy was deleted rather than ported - drift is now impossible, not merely detected. Only\nwire/signing.ts stays local (the HMAC wrappers shared does not carry).\nToolchain: DOWNGRADED to the monorepo's (root ESLint 8 .eslintrc.cjs, TS 5.x, @types/node 20, inherited\nvitest), per the cortex-cli precedent - no own eslint/ts/vitest devDeps. The daemon's custom\nfs-containment lint rules came WITH it as Rule 4 of .eslintrc.cjs (single-resolver invariant), proven\nby clients/bridge/test/lint/containment-rule.test.ts against the ROOT config.\nCI: the daemon's cross-repo workflow folds into ci.yml. Its unit lane rides the workspace test fan-out;\nits heavy canary (mongodb-memory-server + api/dist + the real WS server) is an explicit step after\n`npm run build`, behind a guard asserting the harness entrypoints exist - without it a missing api/dist\nturns the suite into describe.skip and the step passes having tested nothing.\nPackaging: the shipped .tgz cannot resolve the `*` workspace dep and needs shared's RUNTIME (zod values,\nnot just types), so `npm run pack:dist` esbuild-bundles @ekoa/shared into dist/cli/index.js from a\nstaging tree; tsc -b stays what CI typechecks. Everything else stays external and installs on the laptop.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "angle": 0,
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "boundElements": null,
   "containerId": null,
   "fillStyle": "solid",
