   "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-18 (needs_credentials: a first-class run state, its observer, and ensureSession's\ngeneral home). TWO NEW tier-5 modules inside automation/ and ONE new seam file inside cofre/.\n\nautomation/credential-gate.ts - THE general home of ensureSession in the run loop. Until now\nensureSession had exactly ONE caller, the Citius sync rail (routes/sync.ts -> legal/citius-sync.ts),\nso every other integration got no session handling at all: a Rule 3 violation by omission. The gate\nruns before executeStep for a step whose resolveStepDeclaration().credentialRefs is NON-EMPTY -\ndeclaration-driven, never a guess about which sites look like portals, and therefore inert on every\nautomation authored before declarations existed (trap T6). ORIGIN comes from a navigate/api_call\nstep's own URL, an integration step's resolved httpConfig.baseUrl (new seam\nsetIntegrationActionDeclarationResolver, per RUN ACTOR because a key names a different package per\norg), or - for a browser/verify step - the nearest PRECEDING step that answers either. No stored\nallow-list: the discipline the deleted declaredOrigins field left behind. Verdicts: ready (a live\nsession, injected as storageState into a not-yet-created browser), needs-credentials (HALT), or\nneeds-machine (a healthy session with no egress -> routed to the EXISTING awaiting_daemon halt,\nbecause sending a user to the Cofre for a network gap is a lie; P4.1 refines it to blocked).\n\nautomation/credential-waiters.ts - the process-local (org, user, host) -> waiting runIds registry,\npopulated when the engine halts. NOT a second durable truth: the run row is the truth, and this only\nmakes the resume fast. One-shot waiters; PARENT->child origin covering only.\n\ncofre/notify.ts - THE DIRECTION-INVERTING SEAM, and the reason this design is legal at all. The\nCofre has NO event bus (recordCofreEvent is called only from routes/cofre.ts; half the\nCofreRegistoEvent vocabulary is never emitted), so the resume trigger hangs on the DOMAIN functions.\ncofre/ sits BELOW automation/, so cofre/ declares the callback and server.ts binds it to\nautomation/credential-waiters.onCredentialEstablished - exactly setDaemonConnectionResolver. Hooked\nat items.ts mintCofreItem + issueGrant and at integration-items.ts rewriteValue (the in-place\nrotation, the only path the other two do not cover); mintIntegrationCredentialItem,\ncaptureSessionToCofre, captureSessionWithGrant and ensureSession's success all reach the Cofre\nTHROUGH those two and are covered transitively. Pinned by a source assertion that no file in cofre/\nimports automation/.\n\nTHE STATE. needs_credentials joins RunStatus (automation/types.ts + shared/src/automations.ts) and\nAutomationRunEvent (shared/src/events.ts, built by EXTENDING the persisted RunCredentialRequest so\nframe and run resource cannot drift), modelled on awaiting_daemon - HALT AND RE-DISPATCH, never\npaused_for_user's in-process poll, because the human leaves the page. Resume = service.ts\nredispatchRunAwaitingCredentials -> runAutomation with the new additive resumeFromStepIndex, so the\nsteps before the halt are not re-executed. Cross-process (trap T7): server observer + the /cofre\nunlock action's own resume call, both re-reading the durable row, neither load-bearing alone.\n\nP3.2/P3.3. cofre/relay.ts gives RelayPrompt's login variant a PRODUCER and deliberately no\ncompletion half - RelayCompleteRequest.code is an OTP field and there is no typed-OTP automation\nhere (tests/automation/no-typed-otp.test.ts asserts the absence in three layers).\nsession-establishment.ts gains decideReauthRoute: attended is a VETO over any grant, and\ncofre/service.ts hasStandingGrant excludes this_run scope on purpose."
