    "text": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 (P4 ROUND SIX: the fleet seam gains a THIRD answer, and four edges disappear).\n\nSEAM SHAPE CHANGE, which supersedes the DEFAULT DENY sentence in the note above. `automation/\nseams.ts` `EgressCandidateResolver` now answers `EgressCandidate[] | null` instead of\n`EgressCandidate[]`, and its unbound default is `null` rather than `[]`. `null` = this process has no\nlisting; `[]` = the registry answered and this org has no machines. Both refuse selection identically,\nso nothing about egress widens and default-deny holds; what changes is that only the SECOND may be\nread as \"every machine this org had is gone\". `server.ts` binds it to `bridge/registry.ts`\n`egressCandidatesForOrg` unchanged (that function always returns an array). `engine.ts` memoises the\nlisting on `undefined` rather than `null`, so \"not read yet\" and \"no listing\" stop being the same\nstate and the answer cannot depend on call order.\n\nEDGES REMOVED, each because production could not reach it:\n - `locality.ts` -> `egress-policy.ts` `machineRetired`, and with it `locality.ts`'s export of\n   SESSION_MACHINE_RETIRED_REASON (which moved to `egress-policy.ts`, beside the predicate whose\n   `true` produces it). The retirement refusal has ONE producer again: `engine.ts`\n   `credentialGateRecord`. The note above says both sides ask `machineRetired`; only one can.\n - `session-establishment.ts` -> `credential-gate.ts` carrying `establishedByPairingId` on a\n   `reestablished` result. The typist logs in through `getLocalBrowserContext`, i.e. the hosted\n   Chromium, which is on no machine; the field existed only for `EnsureSessionInput.vantage`, which\n   has no production supplier.\n - `legal/citius-sync.ts` deciding its own hosted-typist permit. It takes one as an INPUT now, and\n   `routes/sync.ts` composes it from `automation/origin-posture.ts` `classifyOrigin` - a new\n   routes/ -> automation/ read, in the tier direction, exactly as the run loop does it.\n\nEDGE ADDED. `web/app/(dashboard)/schedules/page.tsx` -> the per-user notifications stream, for\n`schedule_blocked`. The API has emitted that event for every blocked fire since round three and\nnothing in `web/` subscribed to it, so the compensating signal for a neutral (never auto-pausing)\nblock reached nobody.",
    "rawText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 (P4 ROUND SIX: the fleet seam gains a THIRD answer, and four edges disappear).\n\nSEAM SHAPE CHANGE, which supersedes the DEFAULT DENY sentence in the note above. `automation/\nseams.ts` `EgressCandidateResolver` now answers `EgressCandidate[] | null` instead of\n`EgressCandidate[]`, and its unbound default is `null` rather than `[]`. `null` = this process has no\nlisting; `[]` = the registry answered and this org has no machines. Both refuse selection identically,\nso nothing about egress widens and default-deny holds; what changes is that only the SECOND may be\nread as \"every machine this org had is gone\". `server.ts` binds it to `bridge/registry.ts`\n`egressCandidatesForOrg` unchanged (that function always returns an array). `engine.ts` memoises the\nlisting on `undefined` rather than `null`, so \"not read yet\" and \"no listing\" stop being the same\nstate and the answer cannot depend on call order.\n\nEDGES REMOVED, each because production could not reach it:\n - `locality.ts` -> `egress-policy.ts` `machineRetired`, and with it `locality.ts`'s export of\n   SESSION_MACHINE_RETIRED_REASON (which moved to `egress-policy.ts`, beside the predicate whose\n   `true` produces it). The retirement refusal has ONE producer again: `engine.ts`\n   `credentialGateRecord`. The note above says both sides ask `machineRetired`; only one can.\n - `session-establishment.ts` -> `credential-gate.ts` carrying `establishedByPairingId` on a\n   `reestablished` result. The typist logs in through `getLocalBrowserContext`, i.e. the hosted\n   Chromium, which is on no machine; the field existed only for `EnsureSessionInput.vantage`, which\n   has no production supplier.\n - `legal/citius-sync.ts` deciding its own hosted-typist permit. It takes one as an INPUT now, and\n   `routes/sync.ts` composes it from `automation/origin-posture.ts` `classifyOrigin` - a new\n   routes/ -> automation/ read, in the tier direction, exactly as the run loop does it.\n\nEDGE ADDED. `web/app/(dashboard)/schedules/page.tsx` -> the per-user notifications stream, for\n`schedule_blocked`. The API has emitted that event for every blocked fire since round three and\nnothing in `web/` subscribed to it, so the compensating signal for a neutral (never auto-pausing)\nblock reached nobody.",
    "originalText": "AS-BUILT 2026-08-19 (P4 ROUND SIX: the fleet seam gains a THIRD answer, and four edges disappear).\n\nSEAM SHAPE CHANGE, which supersedes the DEFAULT DENY sentence in the note above. `automation/\nseams.ts` `EgressCandidateResolver` now answers `EgressCandidate[] | null` instead of\n`EgressCandidate[]`, and its unbound default is `null` rather than `[]`. `null` = this process has no\nlisting; `[]` = the registry answered and this org has no machines. Both refuse selection identically,\nso nothing about egress widens and default-deny holds; what changes is that only the SECOND may be\nread as \"every machine this org had is gone\". `server.ts` binds it to `bridge/registry.ts`\n`egressCandidatesForOrg` unchanged (that function always returns an array). `engine.ts` memoises the\nlisting on `undefined` rather than `null`, so \"not read yet\" and \"no listing\" stop being the same\nstate and the answer cannot depend on call order.\n\nEDGES REMOVED, each because production could not reach it:\n - `locality.ts` -> `egress-policy.ts` `machineRetired`, and with it `locality.ts`'s export of\n   SESSION_MACHINE_RETIRED_REASON (which moved to `egress-policy.ts`, beside the predicate whose\n   `true` produces it). The retirement refusal has ONE producer again: `engine.ts`\n   `credentialGateRecord`. The note above says both sides ask `machineRetired`; only one can.\n - `session-establishment.ts` -> `credential-gate.ts` carrying `establishedByPairingId` on a\n   `reestablished` result. The typist logs in through `getLocalBrowserContext`, i.e. the hosted\n   Chromium, which is on no machine; the field existed only for `EnsureSessionInput.vantage`, which\n   has no production supplier.\n - `legal/citius-sync.ts` deciding its own hosted-typist permit. It takes one as an INPUT now, and\n   `routes/sync.ts` composes it from `automation/origin-posture.ts` `classifyOrigin` - a new\n   routes/ -> automation/ read, in the tier direction, exactly as the run loop does it.\n\nEDGE ADDED. `web/app/(dashboard)/schedules/page.tsx` -> the per-user notifications stream, for\n`schedule_blocked`. The API has emitted that event for every blocked fire since round three and\nnothing in `web/` subscribed to it, so the compensating signal for a neutral (never auto-pausing)\nblock reached nobody."
  },
  {
    "type": "text",
    "id": "annot-p4-round7-modules-20260819",
    "containerId": null,
    "x": 60,
